  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilient Urban Communities in Asia - BRUC Asia (replace PSIA75)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam is implementing Building Resilience of Urban Communities in Asia Project with funding from the Asian Development Bank under the Urban Climate Change Resilience Trust Fund (UCCRTF). The Urban Resilience Project (URP) is designed to ensure that poor urban dwellers in target cities especially vulnerable groups are able to realize their rights and improve their well -being despite the impact of different shocks and stressors, including climate change. The project works with communities in 10 secondary cities across five countries in doing community -based resilience planning, pilot resilience projects, and influence the local stakeholders to adopt community -led resilience practices. The project is being implemented in Bangladesh, Pakistan, Philippines, Myanmar and Indonesia. The project consortium has Mercy Corps as our partner and they will lead the implementation in Indonesia and Myanmar.    The project activity code IMPA39 is the continuation of PSIA75 under Asian Development Bank (ADB) -BRUC project which was designed to complete the additional deliverables on the contract extension until November 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
